meta {
  name: Security Events
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/events?per_page=25
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  per_page: 25
}

docs {
  The authenticated user's own security log — sign-ins, failed attempts,
  password and two-factor changes, email changes, session revocations —
  newest first, with the IP and user agent behind each one.

  These are the same records that drive the security alert emails, so a
  user can answer "was that me?" without contacting support.

  Paginated: `per_page` defaults to 25 and is capped at 100.
}
